# Deathly Turns — Supplemental Encounters for Wheel of Judgment

**Version:** 0.4
**Source:** Legend of the Five Rings Roleplaying Game — Deathly Turns (supplemental encounters for Wheel of Judgment)
**Publisher:** Fantasy Flight Games

> GM-facing narrative. Boxed **read-aloud** text is reproduced verbatim; intervening GM procedure
> (check TNs, intrigue bookkeeping, branch handling) is summarized faithfully — the full detail lives
> in the source PDF. The statblocks are in `l5r5e-0.4-deathly-turns-cast.ttrpg`, the two new traditions
> in `l5r5e-0.4-deathly-turns-mechanics.ttrpg`, and the encounter structure in
> `l5r5e-0.4-deathly-turns.arc`. These three encounters use the players' own characters — no pregens —
> and the first two presume the PCs have been reincarnated as oni, as in *Wheel of Judgment*. Each can
> also be run apart from that adventure.

---

## Adventure Background

*Deathly Turns* is a supplement of three optional bonus encounters meant to be played in conjunction with the *Wheel of Judgment* adventure, plus an appendix of adventure seeds and two new character traditions. **Blood and Magic** and **Escape of the Hungry Dead** take place in the Spirit Realms and presume the PCs have been reincarnated as oni; **A Mission from Lady Mazoku** takes place in Ningen-dō with conventional mortal PCs. Each also stands alone as a reason to adventure in these strange and dangerous realms.

---

## Encounter 1: Blood and Magic (Jigoku)

The PCs have been reincarnated as oni, using masks provided by the maō (demon lord) **Burakakin**, as in *Wheel of Judgment*; the masks have absorbed their spirits, and they now move relatively freely through the hellish realm of **Jigoku**. Burakakin has given them a task — and in the course of it they come upon the lair of a hulking oni called **the Brute**, attended by three other oni (the **Trio of Vicious Oni**) and conferring with a mysterious figure. Approaching to eavesdrop risks detection (a TN 2 Skulduggery check); the PCs overhear fragments about a mahō-tsukai who claims to have come from a fortress, and about "the Bleak Place."

> The largest oni, a vile figure wrapped in flayed flesh, speaks to its three lesser companions... *...the inside!…from the fortress…the Bleak Place…*

The mysterious figure is **Jya-Aku** ("wickedness"), a mahō-tsukai of prodigious power wearing the **Fel Mantle** — an artifact of dead-oni hide that lets her, a mortal, walk in Jigoku. She carries a leather map to a tunnel from the **Shadowlands** into Rokugan; a mortal trespassing in Jigoku has torn a second passage the PCs may resolve to seal.

### The Course of the Encounter

The PCs may **join forces with (or deceive) the oni** — leaning into their disguise as oni, which for samurai PCs is a profoundly evil act that may cost honor and glory — or fight. The final battle (see **Table 1-1: Oni Battle Scaling** for how many oni to field) pits the PCs against the Brute, the Trio of Vicious Oni, and possibly Jya-Aku. Lecturing the demons on their religious failings (Theology) can weaken their resolve. Winning lets the PCs recover the Brute's **scroll**, whose outside bears a location name freshly scrawled in blood: **the Bleak Place** — a spiritually dead cavern that, uniquely in Jigoku, never shifts, and which the realm's denizens shun.

**Dealing with the Fel Mantle:** the Mantle grants great resistances and Otherworldly status but at a terrible price — constant whispers, a daily loss of composure, and the permanent Shadowlands Taint; if the wearer's composure reaches 0 while wearing it, they are consumed by Fu Leng's will. Removing it flings Jya-Aku back to Ningen-dō through the rock, opening yet another tunnel to seal.

---

## Encounter 2: Escape of the Hungry Dead (Gaki-dō)

Returning toward Meido, the PCs pass through **Gaki-dō**, the Realm of the Hungry Dead, reappearing near the estate of **Hiniku**. Crossing the crowd of gaki (who have no interest in the PCs, as they cannot eat them) requires care — a TN 3+ Courtesy or Command check to avoid running afoul of them.

**Hiniku**, believing the PCs to be oni, is concealing a scheme: she is engineering a **mass escape of gaki into Ningen-dō** through a long-disused passage from Gaki-dō, guarded by a fierce red mazoku warrior named **Hogo-sha** ("guardian"). She offers the PCs rewards — a set of travel papers letting them move freely through Gaki-dō, and forbidden goods — to help her, or simply to refrain from interfering. The PCs may:

- **Accept Hiniku's Offer** — take her papers and travel on.
- **Help Hiniku Engineer the Escape** — deal with Hogo-sha (who cannot simply be persuaded to leave his post; the PCs must bluff, distract, incapacitate, or banish him in combat) and open the passage.
- **Thwart Hiniku's Plans** — dissuade her (an intrigue against Hiniku and her staff, the Mazoku Bureaucrats), subdue or kill her, or inform on her to the mazoku who run the realm.

Interfering with a mass gaki escape into the Mortal Realm has obvious consequences; so does enabling one.

---

## Encounter 3: A Mission from Lady Mazoku (Ningen-dō)

Unlike the first two, this takes place after *Wheel of Judgment*, once the PCs have returned to **Ningen-dō**. The PCs are confronted by **Lady Mazoku**, secret patron of the **Falcon Clan** and its Phantom Hunters, and a magistrate of Gaki-dō who returns escaped spirits to the afterlife on behalf of **Emma-Ō** (were her mortal agents discovered, Emma-Ō would be forced to punish her). She informs the PCs that a dangerous **shade** has escaped the afterlife and — given their recent journey through the underworld — that they are uniquely suited to hunt it, and charges them with finding it and returning it.

### The Shade

The shade is a rōnin duelist who goes by **Hagane** ("steel") — in life **Mirumoto Ikutsuki**, wrongly caused to be exiled from the Dragon Clan years ago, a name he has since forgotten. He now wreaks bloody vengeance on older warriors, wielding his cursed namesake daishō (the katana **Hagane** and wakizashi **Noroi**).

### The Trail of Blood

The PCs first pick up Hagane's trail in the Crane lands, in **Lonely Shore City**: **Kakita Sadao**, old instructor of the Whispering Blade Dōjō, was found dead — his katana deliberately broken — after an unsanctioned duel. A TN 3 Courtesy check convinces the chief magistrate, **Daidoji Himanari**, to share what little the Crane know, including a similar killing of the aged duelist **Doji Yūdai** in Eastern Petal Village near Otosan Uchi. Following the trail (creative checks — Courtesy, Command, Skulduggery, Culture, Government), the PCs realize Hagane is hunting older warriors, and move to protect his next target, **Shiba Akifusa** (with Emihiko). They can lay him to rest by resolving his vengeance, orchestrating a ruse, acquiring spiritual weapons, or an outlandish solution of their own — protecting Akifusa each evening when Hagane attacks. Should his spirit be set to rest, his cursed daishō loses its Unholy quality and becomes **Sacred**.

---

## Appendix: Agents of Mazoku

Adventure seeds building on *A Mission from Lady Mazoku* — agents of the Falcon Clan and of Emma-Ō hunting escaped spirits across Rokugan — plus **two new Bushi traditions** for characters created in the afterlife (see `l5r5e-0.4-deathly-turns-mechanics.ttrpg`):

- **Mazoku's Enforcer Tradition** [Bushi, Sage] — humans "recruited" by overworked mazoku to adjudicate spiritual disputes and uphold Emma-Ō's justice across the realms; the tradition at the foundation of the Falcon Clan.
- **Champion of Days Gone Tradition** [Bushi] — a soul of an ancient age (an archer from the days of Hantei Genji and battles like Regret's Shadow) returned to the living, with the manners, arts, and weapons of a bygone Rokugan.

---

## The Cast at a Glance

- **The Brute** — a hulking, ancient oni that gathered the Trio of Vicious Oni (full statblock). **Trio of Vicious Oni** — three squabbling lesser oni (minion). **Jya-Aku** — a mahō-tsukai in the Fel Mantle, plotting a tunnel into Rokugan (full statblock).
- **Hiniku** — a Gaki-dō bureaucrat engineering a gaki escape (profile-based). **Hogo-sha** — the mazoku guardian of the passage (profile-based).
- **Lady Mazoku** — patron of the Falcon Clan and magistrate of Gaki-dō (full statblock). **Hagane** — the vengeful shade, once Mirumoto Ikutsuki (full statblock).
- **Burakakin** — the maō whose masks reincarnate the PCs as oni. **Emma-Ō** — the Fortune of Death, whose justice Lady Mazoku serves. **Kakita Sadao**, **Doji Yūdai** — Hagane's older-warrior victims. **Shiba Akifusa** — his next target, whom the PCs protect. **Daidoji Himanari** — the Crane magistrate of Lonely Shore City. (Narrative figures.)
